  "verbalization": "Patupilone is implicated in the inhibition of Lysine-specific demethylase 4C (LSD4C) through a shared target of a common compound, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is identified as a target of Patupilone in multiple pathways, suggesting a direct interaction between the drug and the enzyme. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, each linking Patupilone to the same target compound, which in turn targets LSD4C. The high final scores in all three paths indicate a strong, reliable relationship, supported by the shared mechanism of action and the presence of a well-characterized target compound. The mechanism involves the inhibition of LSD4C, which is a key enzyme in the regulation of chromatin structure and gene expression. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Patupilone exerts its biological effects by modulating LSD4C activity, potentially through the inhibition of the target compound.",
